  Lesson(
    id: "geometry",
    number: 9,
    title: "Shaklain — Area, Perimeter aur Angles",
    subtitle: "Baarh ya farsh? Pehle ye pehchano, phir formula khud ayega",
    partIndex: 0,
    partName: "Maths",
    portion: "maths",
    blocks: <LessonBlock>[
      LessonBlock.heading("Ye lesson kyun zaroori hai"),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("PPSC ke one paper me geometry ke sawal har dafa ate hain. Khet ki baarh, kamre ka farsh, gol mez ka kinara, triangle ka teesra kona, ye sawal ghuma phira kar har paper me hain. Aur aik ajeeb baat suno, aksar students formula jante hote hain lekin ghalat formula laga dete hain. Area wale sawal me perimeter nikaal liya, perimeter wale me area. Number concept par nahi, pehchan par kat-te hain. Is lesson ka pehla kaam yahi hai ke tum sawal ko parhte hi pehchan lo ke ye kinare ki baat kar raha hai ya andar ki jagah ki. Phir formula khud yaad ajaye ga."),
      LessonBlock.heading("Perimeter, chaaron taraf ki lambai"),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("Pehle perimeter ko ghar se samajh lo. Tumhare ghar ke sahn ke chaaron taraf baarh lagani hai. Tum kya naapo ge? Sahn ke kinare kinare chal kar kul lambai. Bas yahi perimeter hai, kisi shakal ke chaaron taraf ki kul lambai. Race ke track par aik chakar lagana bhi perimeter hai. Khet ke gird taar lagana bhi perimeter hai."),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("Do baatein pakki kar lo. Perimeter sirf kinara hai, andar ki jagah se is ka koi lena dena nahi. Aur perimeter lambai hai, is liye is ki ikai metre, centimetre ya kilometre hoti hai, seedhi lambai wali."),
      LessonBlock.heading("Area, andar ki jagah"),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("Ab area ko samajh lo. Kamre ke farsh par tiles lagani hain. Tum kya ginoge? Farsh kul kitni jagah gher raha hai. Bas yahi area hai, kisi shakal ke andar ki kul jagah. Carpet aur dari bichhana bhi area hai, aur zameen ka raqba bhi area hai."),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("Area ki ikai perimeter se alag hai, aur yehi farq paper ka phanda hai. Aik tile aik metre lambi aur aik metre chori hoti hai, to wo aik square metre jagah ghirti hai. Area hamesha square me ata hai, square metre ya square centimetre. Zehen me aik tasveer bana lo. Baarh kharidne jao to perimeter socho, tiles kharidne jao to area socho."),
      LessonBlock.image("assets/learning/diagrams/eds/perimeter-area.jpg", caption: "Perimeter versus Area — fence or floor"),
      LessonBlock.heading("Square aur rectangle ke formula, bana kar"),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("Ab formula ratne ki bajaye bana kar dekho. Square, yani murabba, ki chaaron sides barabar hoti hain. Agar aik side 5 metre hai to chaaron taraf ki lambai 5 chaar dafa, yani 4 × 5 = 20 metre. To perimeter barabar 4 guna side. Aur area ke liye socho, farsh par tiles ki 5 kataarein hain aur har kataar me 5 tiles hain, kul 25 tiles. To area barabar side guna side."),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("Rectangle, yani mustateel, me lambaai aur chorai mukhtalif hoti hain. Perimeter me lambaai do dafa ati hai aur chorai bhi do dafa, kyunke samne wali sides barabar hoti hain. Is liye perimeter barabar 2 guna (lambaai jama chorai). Aur area ke liye wahi tiles wali tasveer. Zameen 8 metre lambi aur 5 metre chori hai. Tiles ki 8 wali 5 kataarein bichengi, kul 40 khane. Isi liye area barabar lambaai guna chorai. Guna koi ratta nahi, ye kataaron ka hisaab hai."),
      LessonBlock.heading("Triangle, rectangle ka aadha"),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("Triangle, yani masalas, ka perimeter to seedha hai, teeno sides ka jama. Lekin is ke area me aik raaz hai jo paper bohat azmata hai. Area barabar aadha guna base guna height. Ye aadha aya kahan se?"),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("Aik rectangle lo aur use aik konay se dusre konay tak, yani diagonal par, kaat do. Do triangle bane, aur dono bilkul barabar ke. Matlab har triangle us rectangle ka aadha hisa hai. Rectangle ka area base guna height tha, to triangle ka area us ka aadha ho gaya. Bas, ye aadha kaatne wali tasveer se aya hai, ratne se nahi. Aur aik ehtiyaat, height hamesha wo seedhi lambai hai jo base par seedhi khari ho, yani perpendicular ho. Triangle ka jhuka hua kinara height nahi hota."),
      LessonBlock.heading("Circle aur pi ki kahani"),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("Ab gol shakal par ao. Circle ke teen naam pakke kar lo. Markaz, yani centre, gol ke bilkul beech wala nuqta. Radius wo faasla hai jo markaz se kinare tak ho. Aur diameter wo lakeer hai jo aik kinare se dusre kinare tak markaz se guzar kar jati hai. Diameter hamesha radius ka dugna hota hai, yani d barabar 2r."),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("Circle ka perimeter, jise circumference kehte hain, barabar 2πr hai. Aur is ka area barabar πr² hai. Ab ye π, yani pi, hai kya? Ye is lesson ki sab se pyari baat hai. Koi si bhi gol cheez lo, thaali, plate, gaari ka pahiya. Us ke kinare ke gird dori lapait kar ghera naapo, phir us ka diameter naapo, aur ghere ko diameter se taqseem kar do. Jawab hamesha taqreeban 3.14 ayega. Chhoti thaali ho ya bara pahiya, ye hisaab nahi badalta. Bas isi musalsal jawab ko pi kehte hain, aur paper me is ki qeemat 22/7 li jati hai."),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("Aik pehchan bhi de dun. Jab paper me radius ya diameter 7, 14, 21 ya 28 diya ho, to samajh jao ke sawal 22/7 ke liye bana hai, 7 asaani se kat jaye ga aur hisaab saaf ho jayega."),
      LessonBlock.heading("Angles ki aqsaam"),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("Ab konon, yani angles, ki baat. Kona do lakeeron ke milne se banta hai aur degree me naapa jata hai. Chaar aqsaam paper me bar bar ati hain."),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("Pehla acute angle, nuqeela kona. Ye 90 degree se chhota hota hai. Kainchi ke do hison ke darmiyan wala tang kona zehen me lao. Dusra right angle, theek 90 degree. Tumhari kitaab ka kona, meiz ka kona, yehi right angle hai. Teesra obtuse angle, phaila hua kona. Ye 90 se bara lekin 180 se chhota hota hai, jese zyada khuli hui kitaab ke do safhon ke darmiyan wala kona. Aur chaatha straight angle, theek 180 degree, jo bilkul seedhi lakeer banata hai."),
      LessonBlock.heading("Triangle ke teen konay aur 180 wala raaz"),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("Aakhir me wo baat jo har paper me ati hai. Triangle ke teenon konon ka jama hamesha 180 degree hota hai. Ye bhi ratta nahi hai, is ki tasveer hai. Kagaz ka aik triangle banao. Us ke teeno konay kaat kar alag kar lo. Ab teeno ko aik jagah jor kar seedhi line par rakho. Teeno mil kar aik seedhi lakeer ban jayenge, na kuch zyada, na kuch kam. Aur seedhi lakeer ka kona 180 degree hota hai. Bas yahi se ye qanoon aya hai."),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("Is ka faida seedha hai. Agar triangle ke do konay maloom hon to teesra kona 180 me se dono ka jama ghatta kar nikal ata hai. Paper ka sab se asaan number yahi hota hai."),
      LessonBlock.image("assets/learning/diagrams/eds/triangle-circle.jpg", caption: "Triangle and Circle — the cut-corner trick and pi"),
      LessonBlock.heading("Board par formula"),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("Ustad jab board par is lesson ka khulasa likhta hai to kuch yun likhta hai. Perimeter of a square = 4 × side. Area of a square = side × side. Perimeter of a rectangle = 2 × (length + width). Area of a rectangle = length × width. Perimeter of a triangle = sum of its three sides. Area of a triangle = 1/2 × base × height. Diameter = 2 × radius. Circumference of a circle = 2πr. Area of a circle = πr². π = 22/7. The three angles of a triangle always add up to 180 degrees."),
